# --- CUSTOM ADDITIONS FOR TRADEFLOW ---

# 1. Environment Variables (CRITICAL)
# You already have .env*.local, but you must ignore the main .env file too!
# This prevents your backend API keys and URLs from leaking to GitHub.
.env

# 2. IDE & Editor Folders
# Prevents your personal VS Code or WebStorm settings from overriding your team's
.vscode/
.idea/

# 3. Firebase & Push Notifications (Future-Proofing)
# When you eventually add push notifications for "Order Shipped" alerts,
# these Google configuration files contain sensitive app keys.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# 4. Expo EAS Build output
# If you build the app to share with your friends/testers, it outputs heavy .apk or .tar.gz files here
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.tar.gz
build/
